4. What is JSX?

JSX = JavaScript XML

JSX allows us to write HTML-like syntax inside JavaScript.

Example:

function App() {
    return <h1>Hello World</h1>;
}


<h1>Hello World</h1>

looks like HTML.

But it is actually JSX syntax inside JavaScript.

We can also use JavaScript inside JSX:

const name = "Dhana";

function App() {
    return <h1>Hello {name}</h1>;
}

Output:

Hello Dhana



 
